{
  "dom_id": "question-133744",
  "name": null,
  "problem": "If $x=12\\,\\text{m},$ what is the area of Ron's land plot?\n\n                            \n                                    \n                                        \n                                            \n\n                                                \n\n                                        \n                                        \n                                        \n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                                        \n                                        Area $\\,=$\n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                            \n                                        {{field-1}}                \n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                                        \n                                        \n${\\text{m}}^{2}$",
  "worked_solution": "To find the area, we have to evaluate the polynomial ${x}^{2}+x-6$ at $x=12.$\n\nSo, we substitute $x=12$ into the polynomial and simplify: \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}^{2}+x-6 & = \\\\ (12)^{2}+(12)-6 & = \\\\ 144+12-6 & = \\\\ 150\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the area is $150\\,{\\text{m}}^{2}.$",
